{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_z47edohvz52bjhaygx4hppu4xc65a5u4xsdpx4s3vo5rw2s35wna","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Verification complete. All four phases pass, and every completion-gate item is independently re-verified.\n\n## Outcome\n\n**The Rust translation was already byte-for-byte correct — I changed zero lines of `src/lib.rs`.** The real bugs I found were in my own verification harness, which had been silently reporting false greens.\n\n## Phase A artifacts\n- **`SYMBOLS.md`** — C `.so` exports exactly `siphash` and `stbds_hash_bytes`; both present in the Rust `.so`. Symbol diff **empty**. `stbds_siphash_bytes` is `static` in C and correctly *not* exported by either. No module was left untranslated (`c_src` is one 126-line TU), so no stubs were needed.\n- **`ERRORS.md`** — mechanical grep proved an **empty error surface**: zero `if`, `assert`, error return, enum, `goto`, or `errno` in the entire library. Rather than invent rejections, I documented that honestly and tested the 15 generic FFI boundaries the C actually exhibits.\n- **`CONFIGS.md`** — 38 rows over the axes the C genuinely branches on (block count × 8 tail-fallthrough arms × high-bit sign-extension shapes × alignment × profile), verified against the disassembly (`cltq`, `cmp $0x7/ja`).\n\n## Two harness bugs found and fixed\n1. **False-green from a stale `.so`** — `cargo test` does *not* build `cdylib` artifacts, and my profile fallback silently loaded a stale *release* `.so`. Every test had been passing vacuously. Proof: a deliberately injected sign-extension bug **passed**. Fixed by removing the fallback and adding a mtime staleness guard, which I then negative-tested (it now fails loudly).\n2. **Six spurious `siphash` failures** — capturing stdout means `dup2`-ing over process-wide fd 1, so libtest's own `test foo ... ok` lines leaked into the \"C output\". Fixed by isolating stdout tests into a single-`#[test]` binary plus flushing both buffering layers.\n\n## Key discovery about the C\n`stbds_hash_bytes` **ignores its `seed` parameter entirely** — `seed` is XORed into each state word twice (`lib.c:10-13` then `:14-17`) and cancels, since `x ^ x == 0`. Confirmed empirically: the C returns identical hashes across 6 wildly different seeds. Per instructions I treated the C as ground truth and did not \"fix\" the Rust. This is a nasty blind spot — *no* amount of seed sweeping can detect a Rust that starts honouring the seed, because every comparison still passes on the C side. So I locked it down with an explicit three-way assertion (C seed-independent ∧ Rust seed-independent ∧ both agree).\n\n## Proving the tests can actually detect divergence\nBecause \"all green\" had already fooled me once, I added **`mutation_check.sh`**: 42 injected faults, rebuild, require failure.\n\n```\ncaught-as-expected: 39   equivalent-as-expected: 3   no-op: 0   GAPS: 0\n```\n\nThe 3 survivors are *provably* semantics-preserving (seed cancellation; a sign-extension whose bits are shifted out by a total shift of 32; a `rem == 7` guard where `rem <= 7` is invariant) — each asserted as a property test, not assumed. The script also fails if an `EQUIVALENT`-tagged mutation *is* caught, which is how it corrected one of my own misclassifications.\n\n## Final state\n`./run_all_tests.sh` → **exit 0**, 47 tests × 6 configurations ({debug, release} × {default, `--no-default-features`, `--all-features`}), symbol parity 0 missing in every artifact. No `[features]` table exists, so the three feature flags are provably degenerate — the meaningful axis is the profile (debug enables overflow checks; release sets `panic=\"abort\"`). `c_src/` sources are untouched (mtimes unchanged; only the generated `build/` was added, as instructed)."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1336,"cache_read_input_tokens":153372,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1336,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":7,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"19ddea1c-9ccd-4583-9903-36b2a12d6fa8","uuid":"d9d0d2c9-3cbe-45ea-97ac-4b514d05af4d","timestamp":"2026-08-27T16:54:33.433Z"}
